{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-1520"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Manufacture of footwear"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "1520"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :footwear/manufacturing
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :labor-standards :materials-traceability]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :footwear-plant-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :cae]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "FootwearAdvisor ⊣ Footwear Plant Operations Governor, langgraph-clj
 StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A plant OPERATIONS COORDINATION
 actor for footwear manufacturing (cutting, lasting, assembly lines,
 sole molding) -- not direct cutting/lasting/assembly-line-equipment
 operation authority. Four ops (`:log-production-batch` /
 `:schedule-maintenance` / `:flag-quality-concern` /
 `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect :propose` only. Ten concrete
 governor checks elaborate this blueprint's four HARD invariants:
 propose-only effect, closed op allowlist, closed proposal-effect
 allowlist (no direct cutting/lasting/assembly-line-equipment
 control), permanent direct-operate block, independent equipment
 verification/registration before maintenance scheduling, independent
 batch verification/registration before shipment coordination,
 independent shipment-volume recompute against the batch's own logged
 volume, double-schedule guard, quality-grade validation, and
 defect-rate plausibility validation. Quality-concern flagging
 (materials-defect / labor-safety / labeling-compliance) ALWAYS
 escalates to a human plant supervisor; `:log-production-batch` is the
 only op eligible to auto-commit, and only at phase 3 when
 governor-clean."}
